# Psalms of Solomon — Psalm 8 — The EMET Bible (Literal)
**Translator:** EMET | **Source:** Greek MS (Codex Vindobonensis) | **Section:** Jerusalem's Fall — Sons and Daughters in Grievous Captivity

---

**8:1** Trouble and distress came upon me,
more than all peoples of the earth.

**8:2** Jerusalem heard and was distressed;
and her daughters gave voice to the distress in the land.

**8:3** I put on sackcloth;
I prayed and cried to the LORD,

**8:4** 'What hast thou done against us,
what have we sinned, to bring upon us this punishment?'

**8:5** Thou didst cast our sins upon our necks;
thou didst make them bare upon the neck, for our afflictions.

**8:6** The sons of Israel were scattered abroad in the land of the enemies;
there was no one who redeemed [them].

**8:7** For thou didst drive them out;

**8:8** because the earth was filled with lawless deeds and murders and acts of deceit;
and those who did lawless deeds were numerous in the land.

**8:9** These [things] the LORD saw,
and he hid his face from them, that they should not be pitied.

**8:10** No man, no woman, no infant, not one of their seed,
escaped from the great trouble of the LORD.

**8:11** The heaven was empty [of rain] above them;
the springs of the deep were withheld from them.

**8:12** For over them there were no mountains giving shade,
nor were there hills to give them shelter.

**8:13** Their ways were made desolate [more] than the ways of the east;
those walking in them stumbled [more] than those in darkness.

**8:14** Their sons and daughters were in grievous captivity,
their neck in a seal of slavery.

**8:15** He did to them according to their deeds,
and he handed them over according to their sins.

**8:16** For God turned them over to all the nations [around them],
to be shamed and despised among them.

**8:17** He chose them from all the nations;
now he has rejected them in anger.

**8:18** For except for their God, they had no redeemer;
but the king of the earth, and the just judge, is he.

**8:19** And so he turned me over in my heart's intention to the man from the east;
and thus I bore the yoke of his slavery.

**8:20** I saw him coming against Jerusalem with the armies of the nations,
and his face was terrible.

**8:21** He captured the strong towers and the walls of Jerusalem;
and God let him.

**8:22** The ruler of the nations came to Jerusalem and went up on the heights;
he placed his foot on her neck;

**8:23** and he did not spare her beautiful young men;
he set the young men to the sword.

**8:24** He drove out the exalted of Jerusalem beyond the borders of the land
and sent away the young men to the great sea.

**8:25** And he made the daughter of Jerusalem the mockery of the nations,
and her sons and daughters were in evil captivity.

**8:26** Because the sons of Israel had defiled the holy things of the LORD;
they had profaned with lawless deeds the offerings of God.

**8:27** He set God's altar [before them] as a stone for trampling;
all their glory he turned into shame.

**8:28** He revealed the sins of Jerusalem to the nations;
her beauty was set as spoil before every nation under heaven.

**8:29** He spread her [sins] before the sun in open shame;
and all the earth saw the judgment of God in righteousness.

**8:30** Hidden in secret are the judgments of God in the ends of the earth;
who will know the justice of God except the one who fears him with knowledge?

**8:31** He who understands these things will justify the LORD in his judgments;
he is righteous, and he who does not understand will not speak [against him].

**8:32** For the mercy of the LORD is upon those who fear him,
in judgment to distinguish between the righteous and the sinner.

**8:33** Blessed is the LORD who judges the earth in his righteousness.

**8:34** Israel will praise the LORD by your mercy, O God;
and we shall bless the name of the LORD forever and ever.

---

*EMET notes: Translated from the Greek (Codex Vindobonensis). Hyphenated compounds preserve construct chains. Bracketed words [thus] are implied by grammar but absent from the surface text.*
